title: Remove deprecated polkadot and omni-node CLI flags
doc:
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    Removes CLI flags that were deprecated and no longer had any effect, along with the code that handled them.

    ## Changes

    **polkadot-omni-node**
    - Removes `--experimental-use-slot-based`. Its warning said the flag would be removed after May 2025. Use `--authoring slot-based` instead.
    - `node_extra_args` now takes the authoring policy directly from `--authoring`. The old fallback to `SlotBased` is gone.
    - Updates the omni-node SDK reference docs. They pointed to the removed flag and now link to `--authoring slot-based`.

    **polkadot**
    - Removes `--force-kusama`, `--force-westend` and `--force-rococo`.
    - Chain spec loading from a file path no longer picks a chain-specific spec type based on those flags or on the file name. It always loads a `GenericChainSpec`.
crates:
- name: polkadot-omni-node-lib
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-cli
  bump: patch
